29mj|n|A roll; a scroll; a written document rolled up for keeping or for use, after the manner of the ancients. ; Hence, a collection of printed sheets bound together, whether containing a single work, or a part of a work, or more than one work; a book; a tome; especially, that part of an extended work which is bound up together in one cover; as, a work in four volumes. ; Anything of a rounded or swelling form resembling a roll; a turn; a convolution; a coil. ; Dimensions; compass; space occupied, as measured by cubic units, that is, cubic inches, feet, yards, etc.; mass; bulk; as, the volume of an elephant's body; a volume of gas. ; Amount, fullness, quantity, or caliber of voice or tone.	a:9qv,63,100;olp,62,4;wh6,45,3;dpy,41,1;zfu,36,3;17w6,35,9;raj,34,3;165q,26,5;1klu,21,4;p1c,14,5;ymm,11,3;16ri,3,2~9qv,63,100;17w6,35,9;p1c,14,5;165q,26,5;1klu,21,4;olp,62,4;ymm,11,3;raj,34,3;zfu,36,3;wh6,45,3;16ri,3,2;dpy,41,1	v:dpy,41,1;1tcb,11,8~1tcb,11,8;dpy,41,1	V:vds,22,3~vds,22,3	n:1ark,36,4;rao,35,12;1v5,32,4;1mx4,30,53;1mx8,8,9;1mxc,4,5;1rr7,1,1~1mx4,30,53;rao,35,12;1mx8,8,9;1mxc,4,5;1ark,36,4;1v5,32,4;1rr7,1,1	N:ad4,64,5;1piz,64,9;ad3,61,4;15id,54,1;t0o,37,7;fq4,33,6;aee,33,4~1piz,64,9;t0o,37,7;fq4,33,6;ad4,64,5;aee,33,4;ad3,61,4;15id,54,1
